# ==========================================================================
# Managed by CanonSync — canonical .gitignore (block mode)
# Source of truth: canon/gitignore.master · Do not hand-edit inside a synced repo.
# ==========================================================================

# ==========================================================================
# Canonical .gitignore  --  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is the one file to edit. CanonSync copies the block below into a
# managed region inside every repo's .gitignore.
#
# Do NOT hand-edit the managed block inside an individual repo -- your edit
# will be overwritten on the next sync. Edit THIS file, then run the sync.
# Anything a repo adds OUTSIDE its managed block is preserved untouched.
#
# Add your own project-specific ignores in each repo BELOW the managed
# block (under the "repo-specific ignores" separator), not here.
#
# This template is intentionally generic (no project/ecosystem-specific
# names) so it can be dropped into ANY repo regardless of stack. Sections
# are labeled by language/tool/OS so it's easy to scan, trim, or extend.
# Fully opt-in / commented sections are for stacks that not every repo
# uses (Node, Docker, Terraform, Django, etc.) -- uncomment per-repo below
# the separator, or uncomment here in the master if it should apply to
# every repo going forward.
# ==========================================================================

# --- Python bytecode & caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pyre/
.pytype/
cython_debug/
.tox/
.nox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
htmlcov/
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
*.py,cover
.hypothesis/

# --- Python packaging / distribution ---
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# --- PyInstaller ---
# PyInstaller drops a <name>.spec in the repo root when freezing to an exe.
# Uncomment if your project packages a binary.
# *.spec
*.manifest

# --- Python environment / version managers ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/
.python-version
__pypackages__/
# pipenv: Pipfile.lock is intentionally NOT ignored by default upstream,
# but many teams choose to for apps (not libraries). Uncomment if desired.
# Pipfile.lock
# poetry: same story -- uncomment if this repo treats it as an app, not a lib.
# poetry.lock

# --- Jupyter / IPython ---
.ipynb_checkpoints
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# --- Common Python framework artifacts (opt-in, uncomment if used) ---
# local_settings.py
# db.sqlite3
# db.sqlite3-journal
# instance/
# .webassets-cache
# celerybeat-schedule
# celerybeat.pid
# *.sage.py

# --- Node.js / JavaScript / TypeScript (opt-in section for JS-using repos) ---
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
web_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
lerna-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
.node_repl_history
*.tsbuildinfo
.parcel-cache
.rpt2_cache/
.rts2_cache_cjs/
.rts2_cache_es/
.rts2_cache_umd/
coverage/
.nyc_output
*.tgz
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.yarn/build-state.yml
.yarn/install-state.gz
.pnp.*
# Framework build output (opt-in -- some repos deliberately track these)
# .next/
# .nuxt
# .cache/
# public

# --- Local databases / scratch ---
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-wal
*.db
*.db-journal

